[?2004lFIREWALL FIX SUMMARY
====================

PROBLEM:
Traffic from ML inference service (10.200.0.0/16) could not reach model registry (10.100.0.42:5000)

ROOT CAUSES:
1. Rule was in wrong chain (INPUT instead of FORWARD)
   - Gateway forwards traffic between networks, which uses FORWARD chain
   - INPUT chain only handles traffic destined TO the gateway itself

2. Explicit DROP rules were blocking the traffic
   - Lines blocking all 10.200.0.0/16 -> 10.100.0.0/16 traffic
   - These came BEFORE the general ACCEPT rules, so they took precedence

FIXES APPLIED:
1. Moved port 5000 ACCEPT rule from INPUT chain to FORWARD chain
2. Removed the DROP rules that were blocking inter-network traffic
3. Kept and enhanced bidirectional forwarding rules (eth1 <-> eth2)
4. Made destination more specific (10.100.0.42) for the registry rule

RESULT:
Inference service traffic can now reach the model registry on port 5000
